title: 'C-c d a : skg-delete-references-to-absent-node'
pid: c9a600a2-8720-440e-a2ac-177d67193c30
body: |2-
  On an unknown viewnode, removes that exact raw ID from every owned
  structured relationship in every retained telescope.  It never edits
  foreign telescopes or text links.  If owned title/body text links point at
  the same absent ID, Skg shows a retained warning buffer and asks before the
  structural cleanup; otherwise it runs immediately.  The confirmation is
  bound to the scanned relationships and text links: if they change before
  confirmation, Skg refuses the stale approval and requires a rescan.  Before
  running, save or revert every open skg view.  Afterward, Skg refreshes only
  views which show a changed recorder or the exact absent raw ID.  The
  warning ends by naming skg-investigate-unknown-node (C-c t r), which
  shows what git history knows of the ID.
  Under a skgrepo restriction it refuses ("Deleting the references to an
  absent ID requires no skgrepo restriction"), since it rewrites every
  owned recorder, those the skgrepo restriction keeps out included.
